{
  "slug": "adk-46",
  "name": "Adirondack 46 High Peaks",
  "shortName": "ADK 46",
  "region": "Adirondacks, New York",
  "country": "US",
  "description": "The 46 mountains in the Adirondack Park traditionally listed as over 4,000 feet. Completing them earns membership in the Adirondack Forty-Sixers.",
  "criteria": "The 46 peaks on the traditional (1920s Marshall brothers and Herb Clark) list, using the traditional elevations in use by the Forty-Sixers. No prominence rule applies.",
  "organization": "Adirondack Forty-Sixers (ADK 46ers)",
  "officialUrl": "https://adk46er.org/",
  "notes": "Four peaks on the list (Blake Peak, Cliff Mountain, Nye Mountain, Couchsachraga Peak) are below 4,000 ft according to modern surveys but remain on the list as originally defined; the 46ers still count them. Winter 46er: winter is astronomical winter, from the December solstice (Dec 21) to the March equinox (Mar 21); the club FAQ states Dec 21 to Mar 21 inclusive. A Winter 46er climbs all 46 peaks in that window; a winter round alone qualifies for registration (a 'W' is added to the 46er number), and winter climbs also count toward the regular round. Elevations are the traditional list values from Wikipedia's table; ties (Gray/Iroquois 4,840; Armstrong/Hough 4,400; Big Slide/Esther 4,240; Blake/Cliff 3,960) are ranked in table order. Range names other than 'Adirondack High Peaks' are common groupings, not taken from a cited table.",
